<title>GREECE: GREEK JAN INFLATION FALLS TO 6.8PCT Y/Y- SOURCE.</title>
<headline>GREEK JAN INFLATION FALLS TO 6.8PCT Y/Y- SOURCE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's consumer price inflation fell to 6.8 percent year-on-year in January, a monetary source told Reuters.</p>
<p>The inflation figure is based on a revised CPI index used for calculation purposes for the first time in January.</p>
<p>Greek inflation stood at 7.5 percent year-on-year in December based on the old version of the CPI index.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
